* THS4541 fully differential amplifier: a behavioural macro model written for
* CopperLib in the PSpice dialect (VALUE, LIMIT, IF, I() probes,
* R_NOISELESS). It is not TI's model. Figures from the THS4541 data sheet
* SLOS375B (August 2014, revised February 2024),
* https://www.ti.com/lit/ds/symlink/ths4541.pdf,
* sha256 89116b7887557237335675481ed80c5f3570b4d920d0b882393a877fb1796765
* (the part's source_checksum), typical values at 5 V, 25 C, section 6.5:
*   open-loop gain     119 dB (1 mS into 891 kohm)
*   gain-bandwidth     850 MHz, dominant pole about 900 Hz (8.3.1, p. 35)
*   second pole        FP2, fitted to the -3 dB bandwidths of 6.5 at
*                      G = 1, 2, 5 and 10 (RF = 402 ohm) and the 10 %
*                      overshoot at G = 2; see the part file
*   slew rate          1500 V/us, differential (the input stage limited)
*   voltage noise      2.2 nV/rtHz differential, white (a 292 ohm thermal
*                      resistor in IN+); its 100 kHz 1/f corner is not modelled
*   current noise      1.9 pA/rtHz on each input, white (a 4.59 kohm thermal
*                      resistor bootstrapped to its input, so it carries no
*                      signal current); its 1 MHz 1/f corner is not modelled
*   input              110 kohm || 0.85 pF differential; 10 uA bias current
*                      out of each input (PNP inputs); common-mode range and
*                      CMRR not modelled
*   output             0.2 V from either rail (RL = 499 ohm); 1.5 ohm per
*                      output, fitted to the 0.1 ohm closed-loop output
*                      impedance at 10 MHz, G = 2; no current limit (8.3.1:
*                      the part has none)
*   common mode        Vocm sets the output average with gain 1 (0.982 in
*                      6.5) through a 150 MHz pole (Vocm small-signal
*                      bandwidth); 100 kohm to each rail and 1.2 pF set the
*                      open-pin default to mid-supply (8.3.1; 6.5 gives
*                      47 kohm || 1.2 pF)
*   supply current     10.1 mA quiescent plus the output currents from the
*                      rail that sources them; PSRR not modelled
* FB+ and FB- are joined to OUT+ and OUT- inside (8.3.1: the RGT package's
* feedback outputs). PD is not modelled: the part is always on.
* Pins: FB-, IN+, IN-, FB+, Vs+, Vocm, OUT+, OUT-, Vs-.
.SUBCKT THS4541_BEHAVIOURAL FBM INP INM FBP VP VOCM OUTP OUTM VN
.PARAM GM=1M A0=891K GBW=850MEG FP2=3G SR=1500E6 RSW=0.2 RO=1.5 IQ=10.1M IB=10U
.PARAM CP={GM/(2*PI*GBW)} IMAX={SR*CP}
* Inputs: voltage noise, bootstrapped current noise, differential impedance, bias.
R_EN INP N_INP 292
R_INP INP N_BTP 4.59K
E_BTP N_BTP 0 INP 0 1
R_INM INM N_BTM 4.59K
E_BTM N_BTM 0 INM 0 1
R_DIFF N_INP INM R_NOISELESS 110K
C_DIFF N_INP INM 0.85P
I_BP VN INP {IB}
I_BM VN INM {IB}
* Differential stage: slew-limited transconductance into the dominant pole,
* then the second pole.
G_IN 0 N_P VALUE={LIMIT(GM*V(N_INP,INM), -IMAX, IMAX)}
R_P N_P 0 R_NOISELESS {A0/GM}
C_P N_P 0 {CP}
E_P2 N_P2A 0 N_P 0 1
R_P2 N_P2A N_P2 R_NOISELESS 1K
C_P2 N_P2 0 {1/(2*PI*1K*FP2)}
* Common mode: the Vocm pin's default divider and the common-mode loop's pole.
R_CMT VP VOCM 100K
R_CMB VOCM VN 100K
C_VOCM VOCM 0 1.2P
E_CMA N_CMA 0 VOCM 0 1
R_CM N_CMA N_CM R_NOISELESS 1K
C_CM N_CM 0 {1/(2*PI*1K*150MEG)}
* Outputs: the common mode plus and minus half the differential, within the
* swing limits, through the output resistance and a current sense each.
E_OP N_OP 0 VALUE={LIMIT(V(N_CM)+V(N_P2)/2, V(VN)+RSW, V(VP)-RSW)}
E_OM N_OM 0 VALUE={LIMIT(V(N_CM)-V(N_P2)/2, V(VN)+RSW, V(VP)-RSW)}
R_OP N_OP N_SP R_NOISELESS {RO}
V_SP N_SP OUTP 0
R_OM N_OM N_SM R_NOISELESS {RO}
V_SM N_SM OUTM 0
R_FBP OUTP FBP R_NOISELESS 0.01
R_FBM OUTM FBM R_NOISELESS 0.01
* Supply currents: the quiescent current and each output's current from the
* rail that sources it.
G_Q VP VN VALUE={IQ}
G_SRCP VP 0 VALUE={IF(I(V_SP) > 0, I(V_SP), 0)}
G_SNKP 0 VN VALUE={IF(I(V_SP) < 0, -I(V_SP), 0)}
G_SRCM VP 0 VALUE={IF(I(V_SM) > 0, I(V_SM), 0)}
G_SNKM 0 VN VALUE={IF(I(V_SM) < 0, -I(V_SM), 0)}
.MODEL R_NOISELESS RES (T_ABS=-273.15)
.ENDS THS4541_BEHAVIOURAL
